From d3fca336e6c7262385d7042a2f6465e7529effb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:23:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Trip builder: edit your trip any way you like, before and
 after you send it

Front end (ships with the site):
- "Start building" is always a blank sheet, with a short walk-around of the real controls. The trip
  you had is kept: the home page offers "Pick up where you left off".
- Clear, worded Remove stop / Swap place buttons on every stop, removable tour chips, a big
  "+ Add another stop" at the end of the list, and an add picker that asks where the stop goes.
- The day-by-day plan is editable (move a tour to another day, add one, remove one).
- Undo / Redo for everything, including "Start over". One validated, all-or-nothing editing layer.

Guests can change a trip after sending it, until it is booked (new function trip-builder-revise):
- The change REPLACES the trip on the same request (same ref, deposit, beds held), so the crew never
  reviews a plan the guest has moved on from. The crew gets an UPDATED email with what moved; an
  approval is withdrawn if the plan changes after it; a booked or declined trip can't be changed here.
- The crew's review page shows what the guest changed, and refuses to approve / decline / edit a
  version the guest has since changed (409 stale).
- No migration, no new secret, no running cost. The guest key is handed to their browser when they send
  the trip and is in their deposit email's trip link.

Tests: _shared/trip-builder-revise.test.ts (10), e2e 79 checks (26 new for guest changes).
See docs/trip-builder-revise.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
